# Troubleshooting

## `URL_SCHEME_NOT_SUPPORTED` or a `turso:` error

Use the Turso **libSQL** URL, starting with `libsql://`. A `turso://` URL belongs to the newer Turso Database engine and is not supported by this app's libSQL driver.

## `503 setup_required` on a deployment

The database has no password and no `L30_INITIAL_PASSWORD` was set. Add an 8+ character initial password to the environment and restart or redeploy.

## `403 reset_local_only`

Reset is disabled on deployments. Use the recovery steps in [passwords and recovery](/docs/passwords).

On a local install, the request did not come from the same machine. Open `/reset` on the machine running the reader.

## Port already in use

The packaged app tries 4477 through 4487. Set `PORT` to pin another port:

<CopyCommand command="PORT=4480 last30days" />

For development, pass a port to Vite:

<CopyCommand command="pnpm exec vite dev --port 4480" />

## Vercel feed is empty

Open the app and refresh. The first refresh fetches items; AI summaries are optional. If refresh fails, check the Turso URL and token in the Vercel project.

## Docker data disappears

Mount a volume at `/data`. The container warns when `/data` is not mounted. Without a volume, the database lives inside the container and disappears when it is removed.

## The install command shows `localhost`

The landing was built without `APP_URL`. Set `APP_URL` in the landing Vercel project and redeploy. See [configuration](/docs/configuration#landing-app-url).

## Node version is rejected

The installers and the package require Node.js exactly `26.13.0`. Install that version from [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org) and run the command again.

